  "recap": "The Base Invaders fell 20-8 to the Hitmen on Wednesday, July 29, in a game where the bats were far from silent but couldn't keep pace with a relentless Hitmen offense. The team pounded out 21 hits and got 9 players on base, showing real life throughout the lineup, but too many of those baserunners were left stranded as the deficit grew. Scotty led the charge going 4-for-5 with 2 RBI, and Jason matched him with a 4-for-5 night of his own. Dillon chipped in 2-for-4 with 2 RBI, while Brendan (2-for-5, 1 RBI) and Keith (1-for-5, 1 RBI) added to the offensive effort. It was the kind of night where individual performances shone even as the team result didn't go their way, and the Base Invaders will look to tighten things up on the other side of the ball next time out.",
